# Environment for examples/decombat-lobby.service (EnvironmentFile=/opt/decombat/config/decombat.env). WRITTEN ON
# WINDOWS, NEVER RUN. tools/vps/bootstrap.sh copies it once and sets DC_SERVER__ADVERTISE_IP from --public-ip.
# DC_<SECTION>__<KEY> overrides the same key of server.toml (precedence: flag > environment > server.toml).
# The address clients are told to connect to (the VPS public IPv4 address); bootstrap.sh --public-ip writes the
# line uncommented. Without it the toml's 127.0.0.1 stays and the lobby refuses to start with --public (LG-31).
#DC_SERVER__ADVERTISE_IP=<VPS public IPv4 address>
# The paths are already in examples/server-vps.toml; these lines also let examples/server.toml (Windows paths) run.
DC_PATHS__ROM=/opt/decombat/rom
DC_PATHS__DB=/opt/decombat/data/ca.db
DC_PATHS__LOG_DIR=/opt/decombat/logs
# The lobby passes the ROM folder to every dc-dserver it starts; CA_ROM is only read by dc-server-rom --verify.
RUST_BACKTRACE=1
# Read by tools/vps (status.sh, bots.sh, instance.sh), not by the lobby (no __, so not config). The default instance's
# admin address is the unit's --admin flag (127.0.0.1:10090); a named instance's decombat.env (instance.sh create)
# carries DC_ADMIN=127.0.0.1:<its port>, which decombat-lobby@.service passes as --admin, and DC_BOT_LOBBY.
#DC_ADMIN=127.0.0.1:10090
#DC_BOT_LOBBY=127.0.0.1:10000
